{
  "about": "Public model registry: role -> model, backup, route and USD per 1M tokens (priceCached = cache read, priceWrite = 5-minute cache write; longPrompt = the rate card for prompts over overTokens input tokens). via: the role's declared route, checked at boot (an xai role must run grok; an openrouter role's model and backup need an OpenRouter id). The route follows the model: every grok call goes to xAI direct (server-side search, web_search / x_search, exists only there), every Claude call through OpenRouter, pinned to Anthropic with no provider fallback; while xAI is down (3 failures in a row, for 10 min) or keyless, a grok call without search goes through OpenRouter pinned to xAI, the same model id. openrouter: our model id -> its OpenRouter id. The backup is the model a swap falls back to; there is no automatic failover. Sources: docs.x.ai/docs/models (grok, checked 2026-10-07), platform.claude.com/docs/en/about-claude/pricing (Claude, checked 2026-10-08), openrouter.ai/api/v1/models (ids, prices and the grok long-prompt rate, checked 2026-10-09). A model with no price, or not listed here, is charged the priciest listed rate. Changes go through a public tryout and a model-change record (docs/MODELS.md).",
